Privacy Policy for Productivity Enhancer

Last Updated: August 26, 2026

Productivity Enhancer ("the Extension") is a Chrome browser extension that provides optional webpage customization features and educational resource shortcuts.

Information We Collect

Productivity Enhancer does not collect, transmit, sell, or share personal information.

The Extension does not operate a server, analytics system, advertising system, user account system, or database for collecting user information.

Information Stored Locally

The Extension uses Chrome's local storage functionality to remember which features the user has enabled or disabled.

These settings are stored locally in the user's browser and are not transmitted to the developer or any third party.

Webpage Access

Productivity Enhancer requires access to webpages in order to provide its user-selected features. Depending on which features are enabled, the Extension may modify webpage content or behavior, including images, text, colors, scrolling, links, and visual effects.

The Extension does not intentionally collect or transmit webpage content, browsing history, passwords, form data, or other personal information.

Bookmarks

The Extension includes an optional feature that allows the user to add a predefined collection of educational resources to their Chrome bookmarks.

This feature only creates the bookmarks when the user explicitly selects the corresponding button. The Extension does not read, collect, upload, or analyze the user's existing bookmarks.

Third-Party Services

Some Extension functionality may cause the browser to request resources from third-party websites, such as externally hosted images, fonts, or links selected by the user.

Productivity Enhancer does not control the privacy practices of those third-party services. Users should review the privacy policies of those services if they have concerns about requests made by their browser.

Data Security

Because Productivity Enhancer does not collect or maintain personal information on developer-controlled servers, there is no developer-controlled database of user information to protect.

Local settings are managed through Chrome's built-in extension storage mechanisms.

Children's Privacy

Productivity Enhancer is not intended to collect personal information from children or adults. The Extension does not knowingly collect personal information from any user.

Changes to This Privacy Policy

This Privacy Policy may be updated if the Extension's functionality or data practices change. Any updated version will be published at this location with a revised "Last Updated" date.

Contact

For questions about this Privacy Policy or Productivity Enhancer, please contact the developer through the contact information provided on the Extension's Chrome Web Store listing.

Productivity Enhancer does not collect or sell user data.
